<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Voccio</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. 60–49 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a> · Also known as King Voccio</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Voccio was a king of Noricum in the mid-1st century BCE, the only Norican ruler known by name from Roman writers. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/julius-caesar">Julius Caesar</a> records that his sister married the Germanic leader <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ariovistus">Ariovistus</a>, and that in 49 BCE Voccio sent 300 cavalrymen to support Caesar in the civil war against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pompey">Pompey</a>. His reign shows Noricum as a friendly client state of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>.</p></div>
